course: dictionary
lesson: 12779
title: Effects: changes and results
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An effect is what happens because of something else. The thing that makes it happen is the cause. «The sun was hot all day, and the ice on the pond melted.» The hot sun is the cause, and the melted ice is the effect.
explain: Effects is the plural of effect, so it means more than one result or change. Look at the words around it for clues. «The special effects in the film made the dragon look real.» The words special and film tell you that effects are the clever sounds, lights or pictures that make a film exciting.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. «Eating fresh fruit has a good effect on your health.» Does changes or results still make sense? Yes, so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: «Effects» means changes or results that happen because of something.
fact: «Special effects» are sounds, lights or pictures made for films, plays and games.
fact: «Side effects» are extra results of a medicine, such as feeling sleepy.
fact: «Cause and effect» means the thing that makes something happen, and the thing that happens because of it.
fact: In a formal, old-fashioned way, «effects» can mean a person's belongings.
exercise: «Heat had effects on the ice, and it melted.» What does effects mean here? | Loud noises from a film | *Changes that happen because of the heat | Cold, hard things | A person's belongings
exercise: «The special effects made the dragon look real.» What are special effects? | The shoes an actor wears | Sweets given out at a party | Stories told by the teacher | *Sounds, lights or pictures made for films and games
exercise: «The rain fell, so the path was wet.» What is the effect? | Umbrellas were sold | The rain fell | The sky was blue | *The path was wet
test: «The medicine had side effects, so Sam felt sleepy.» What are the side effects? | Names of the doctors who work at the clinic | *Extra results of the medicine, like feeling sleepy | Ways to make the medicine taste nice
test: What does «have an effect on» mean? | To hide something | To count something carefully | *To change something | To look at something closely
exam: In «The plant grew tall because it had sun», what is the cause? | *It had sun | Tall | The plant grew tall | Plants are green
